<SiteLayout title="Privacy" description="How the Teton County guide handles listing suggestions, contact details, and website analytics." path="/privacy/">
<section class="section prose">
<span class="eyebrow">YOUR DETAILS STAY YOURS</span>
<h1>Privacy, plainly.</h1>
<p>Last updated October 20, 2026.</p>
<h2>When you send a suggestion</h2>
<p>We collect the name, email, listing details, and message you submit, plus the request time and review status. These are stored privately for the guide team to review your request and respond. Your email is not published in the directory or added to a rental marketing list.</p>
<p>We also send your submission to Formspree, which stores it in the guide team's private inbox and sends an email notification to the editor. Your email is used as the reply address so the editor can respond. No marketing subscription is created.</p>
<h2>When you ask about housing</h2>
<p>The corporate housing page has a separate inquiry form. We collect whether you are an employer or an individual, your name, email, optional phone number, company, number of apartments, bedrooms, move-in date, expected length of stay, and any message you add, plus the request time. Housing inquiries are stored privately and sent to a separate private Formspree inbox. They are read by the guide’s editor, the same person who reviews suggestions, so no other company receives them.</p>
<p>We use your housing inquiry only to reply about renting at <SponsorLink placement="privacy_housing">Teton Flats</SponsorLink>, the guide’s sponsor. It is not added to a marketing list, and no marketing subscription is created. Housing inquiries are intended to be deleted within 12 months after receipt.</p>
<h2>Spam protection and hosting</h2>
<p>The site uses Cloudflare hosting and, when the submission service is configured, Cloudflare Turnstile to limit automated spam. Cloudflare processes network and browser information to operate these services. The form service stores a short-lived, one-way network identifier for rate limiting rather than storing a raw IP address in the request record.</p>
<h2>Maps and outside websites</h2>
<p>Interactive maps load OpenStreetMap tiles only when you choose the map view. Those requests reveal normal connection information to the map provider. Links to business websites and <SponsorLink placement="inline_text">Teton Flats</SponsorLink> open services with their own privacy policies.</p>
<h2>Website analytics</h2>
<p>Cloudflare Web Analytics measures page visits and website performance to help us improve the guide.</p>
<p>We use Google Analytics to understand which pages people visit and how they use the guide. Google Analytics uses cookies and collects information such as pages viewed, referral sources, interactions, and browser and device details. When you follow a link to our sponsor’s website, we record which link on which page you used, and the link itself identifies this guide as the referring site. We do not send the names, email addresses, or message text entered into our forms to Google Analytics.</p>
<p>Learn <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>. You can control cookies through your browser settings or use Google's <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>
<h2>Retention and requests</h2>
<p>Submission records in Cloudflare, Formspree, and notification emails are intended to be deleted within 12 months after review. Short-lived rate-limit records expire after one day and are cleaned up as requests arrive. To request access, correction, or deletion, use the <a href="/suggest/?type=contact">contact form</a> and identify your earlier request. Do not include sensitive information.</p>
</section>
</SiteLayout>
